                <pb facs="1025" n="875" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg875"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister to
                        Minister Gummeré.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-02-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 16,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister and Dear Colleague</hi>: I have the
                    honor to acknowledge the receipt of your letter of the 15th instant, in reply to
                    that which I have addressed to you the 4th of this month on the subject of the
                    protection of patents of inventions in Morocco.</p>
                <p>In thanking you for the prompt attention that you have given to the matter, I
                    beg, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard Lowther.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
